st request in both save paths.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/common/data.resource.ts:527-553`, `createOrUpdateVitalsAndBiometrics`.\n\n**Likely affected, not verified**\n\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/vitals-biometrics-form/vitals-biometrics-form.test.tsx` has `signal` assertions at lines 280 and 437. I did not read the surrounding code, so I can't say whether they depend on abort behaviour or only on the presence of a signal.\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/mock.tsx:108` and `mock-jest.tsx:103` mock the hook for tests. Any test that relies on the mock mirroring real behaviour would be affected, but I have not checked which tests do.\n\n**Not checked**\n\n- I searched references only in `openmrs-esm-patient-chart`. The other 12 `openmrs-esm-*` repositories listed by Falkon were not searched, so any other app using the hook is not covered here.\n- Dynamic use, such as re-exports through `@openmrs/esm-framework` in other packages, would not show up in name searches.\n- I did not read the lab-results and vitals test files, so I have not confirmed how they exercise the controller.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useAbortController.ts\", \"startLine\": 25, \"endLine\": 38},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/lab-results/exported-lab-results-form.workspace.tsx\", \"startLine\": 70, \"endLine\": 70},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/lab-results/exported-lab-results-form.workspace.tsx\", \"startLine\": 240, \"endLine\": 340},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/vitals-biometrics-form/exported-vitals-biometrics-form.workspace.tsx\", \"startLine\": 87, \"endLine\": 87},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/vitals-biometrics-form/exported-vitals-biometrics-form.